- ### Syllables
+ ### Sillabe

- `syllables` splits text into its parts. Each syllable is a segment, and each run of
- characters which are not letters passes through as a segment of its own:
+ `syllables` divide il testo nelle sue parti. Ogni sillaba è un segmento, e ogni sequenza di
+ caratteri che non sono lettere passa come segmento a sé:

= characters which are not letters passes through as a segment of its own:
